1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,083
Every morning, before the city woke,

2
00:00:04,083 --> 00:00:08,891
my grandmother spread
fresh grass on the floor.

3
00:00:09,891 --> 00:00:17,882
She washed the green beans slowly.
She never rushed coffee.

4
00:00:18,882 --> 00:00:26,333
Then came the fire, and the smell
that called the neighbours in.

5
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:34,694
Incense filled the room.
It was her way of saying: welcome.

6
00:00:35,694 --> 00:00:40,725
The sound of pounding was
the first music of my day.

7
00:00:41,725 --> 00:00:48,686
Then we waited. She taught me
that waiting is part of the gift.

8
00:00:49,686 --> 00:00:55,127
One pot. Many cups.
No one was ever left out.

9
00:00:56,186 --> 00:01:03,347
Three rounds: abol, tona,
and bereka, the blessing.

10
00:01:04,347 --> 00:01:08,308
By the third cup,
strangers had become family.

11
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:14,868
'Stay a little longer,' she always
said. 'The coffee is still warm.'
